.TH EUCLID-CLI-EKM-DECRYPT 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.33" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-ekm-decrypt \- decrypt a file or stdin with an encryption key
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli ekm decrypt
.BR \-\-key\-id | \-k
.I KEY_ID
[\fB\-\-input\fR|\fB\-i\fR \fIFILE\fR]
[\fB\-\-output\fR|\fB\-o\fR \fIFILE\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Decrypts a file or, if
.B \-\-input
is omitted, standard input, with the given key and writes the
recovered plaintext to a file or, if
.B \-\-output
is omitted, standard output. The input must be ciphertext produced by
.BR euclid-cli-ekm-encrypt (1)
with the same key.
.PP
Unlike most
.B ekm
actions, the request and response bodies are raw bytes rather than
JSON: the ciphertext travels as the request body and the plaintext
comes back as the response body, both read and written in binary
mode. The key ID travels as a header instead of a JSON field.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-key\-id " " \fIKEY_ID\fR
ID of the key to decrypt with, as returned by the
.B name
field of
.BR euclid-cli-ekm-create-key (1).
Must be the same key that was used to encrypt the data. Required.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-input " " \fIFILE\fR
Path of the file to decrypt. If omitted, the ciphertext is read from
standard input.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIFILE\fR
Path to write the recovered plaintext to. If omitted, the plaintext
is written to standard output.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The data was decrypted and verified; the plaintext was written to the
requested destination.
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments, the input or output file could not be
opened, the server could not be reached, or the server rejected the
request (unknown key ID, wrong key, or the ciphertext was truncated
or tampered with).
.SH EXAMPLES
Decrypt a file back to another file:
.PP
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 ekm decrypt \e
    --key-id 3f1c2b7a-... --input plain.enc --output plain.txt
.fi
.RE
Decrypt stdin and write plaintext to stdout:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cat plain.enc | euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 \e
    ekm decrypt --key-id 3f1c2b7a-... > plain.txt
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-ekm (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ekm-create-key (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ekm-list-keys (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ekm-revoke-key (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ekm-delete-key (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ekm-encrypt (1)
